<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 December, from 1508 to 1948.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">Human Rights Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed on the anniversary of the UN General Assembly's adoption of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights in 1948, Human Rights Day reaffirms the inalienable rights and fundamental freedoms to which every person on Earth is entitled.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-cambrai" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/league-of-cambrai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1508 CE <span class="tih-ago">518 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The League of Cambrai is formed against Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a>, Emperor Maximilian I and Ferdinand of Aragon formally concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-cambrai">League of Cambrai</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Routed at Agnadello in 1509, Venice had recovered most of its mainland territory by 1516.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1520">1520 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">506 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luther burns the papal bull against him</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>'s Elster Gate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> burned Leo X's bull threatening him with excommunication, along with books of canon law. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> excommunicated him the following month.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1541">1541 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">485 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Culpeper and Francis Dereham are executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Culpeper, a close friend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> accused of adultery with Queen Catherine Howard, was beheaded for treason. Francis Dereham, whose involvement with Catherine before her marriage to the king had been discovered, was also executed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1665">1665 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">361 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dutch Regiment de Marine is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The grand pensionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-de-witt">Johan de Witt</a> and Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michiel-de-ruyter">Michiel de Ruyter</a> established the Regiment de Marine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> Marine Corps, the second-oldest marine corps still active, traces its origins to it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michiel-de-ruyter">Michiel de Ruyter</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1817">1817 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">209 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mississippi becomes the 20th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> was admitted to the Union. Its fertile lands became the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> economy built on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, and later a key battleground of the civil rights movement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wyoming Territory gives women the vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor John Campbell signed a law granting women in Wyoming Territory the right to vote and hold office, the first such law in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Wyoming is still called the 'Equality State'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Nobel dies in San Remo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-nobel">Alfred Nobel</a>, the Swedish chemist who invented dynamite, died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. His will left most of his fortune to fund prizes, first awarded on the anniversary of his death in 1901.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The UN adopts the Universal Declaration of Human Rights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the UN General Assembly adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-declaration-of-human-rights">Universal Declaration of Human Rights</a> without a vote against. The drafting committee was chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 10 December <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gaston-de-foix-duke-of-nemours"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gaston-de-foix-duke-of-nemours.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gaston de Foix, Duke of Nemours</span><span class="tp">1489–1512</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/c-rajagopalachari"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">C. Rajagopalachari</span><span class="tp">1878–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-manley"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Michael Manley</span><span class="tp">1924–1997</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 10 December <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paolo-uccello"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paolo-uccello.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paolo Uccello</span><span class="tp">1397–1475</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-ii-duke-of-lorraine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-ii-duke-of-lorraine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René II, Duke of Lorraine</span><span class="tp">1451–1508</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sakamoto-ryoma"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sakamoto-ryoma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sakamoto Ryoma</span><span class="tp">1836–1867</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfred-nobel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfred-nobel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfred Nobel</span><span class="tp">1833–1896</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nikola-pasic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nikola-pasic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nikola Pašić</span><span class="tp">1845–1926</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/augusto-pinochet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Augusto Pinochet</span><span class="tp">1915–2006</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
